This licence covers every file in playerkit/ that carries the "Copyright
CBOC-Vita" header. playerkit is new code written for this project. It contains
no code copied or adapted from gpsp/ (GPL), from xBRZ, or from any other
GPL-licensed source, so that it can be linked into programs that carry a
licence which is not GPL-compatible (the Snes9x-based SNES player). Where the
VitAdhoc interface was matched (labels, colours, file layouts, behaviour), it
was matched by observing the finished program's behaviour and reading its
user documentation and UI code for appearance, labels and file formats; no
expression was carried over and every line here was written fresh.

Dependencies: the C++11 / C99 standard library only. Platform code sits
behind small interfaces (pk_gfx, the file operations in pk_fs) and is
isolated in playerkit/vita/ (vita2d and the PS Vita SDK headers, both MIT).

playerkit/src/pk_font_data.cpp holds glyph bitmaps rasterised from Inter and
Outfit, which are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (see
playerkit/fonts/). playerkit/tools/gen_font.cpp uses stb_truetype (public
domain / MIT) from snes/frontend/third_party/stb, only to regenerate that
file; it is not linked into any player.
